caption: Supernatural Origins
technology-rule: supernatural-origins

Any supernatural advantage granted by a chem must include exactly one GATES origin modifier: Force, Psi, Magic, Divine, Cinematic, or Super. Each origin modifier is worth -10%.

Apply the origin modifier normally when calculating Design Point Load and Benefit Value. The origin modifier does not remove or reduce the extraordinary-trait multipliers to Design Point Load or Level Load.

All supernatural components of one integrated Chem normally share the same origin. Mixed-origin packages require explicit GM approval.

Each major technological tradition or central technology hub should define one or two native Chem origins. A designer may create Chems using those native origins normally. Creating a Chem with any other origin requires Weird Science in addition to the normal design skills. For example, Fallout-derived pharmaceutical technology natively supports Cinematic Chems, while BioShock-derived technology natively supports Super Chems.

A supernatural origin affects SPAA, suppression, Neutralize, Static, countermeasures, and similar interactions. It never changes the Chem's classification as a Temporary Physical buff.

The origin determines which setting-specific countermeasures, suppressors, Neutralize effects, Static effects, and similar defenses can affect the chem-granted ability.

The default duration is one minute.

The designer may select an appropriate onset and delivery method, such as:

Injection

Inhaler

Pill or capsule

Dermal patch

Contact agent

Aerosol

Implant reservoir

At TL9, onset and delivery method are normally design choices rather than point modifiers. Particularly advantageous or restrictive forms may require GM approval or appropriate GURPS modifiers.
